```

## Summary by scenario

The table lists every scenario of this report with the number of comparisons it made
against reference values (*Checks*) and the number of recorded outcomes that failed
(*Failures*).

  * For the plasma, urine and pharmacodynamics scenarios a failure is a comparison outside
    the acceptance criteria.
  * `PKG-TEST` makes no numeric comparison. Its single recorded outcome is the result of the
    package test suite, so its *Checks* value is zero, and a failure of `PKG-TEST` means the
    test suite failed.
  * A required scenario whose code chunk errored out produces no rows and is listed as NOT
    REPORTED. The results table of such a scenario is also absent from the Results chapter.

The integration method is named in the table by its `calcm` value (`:lint`, `:luld`,
`:logt`, `:luldt`). The abbreviation `dt` denotes the dose time. The Results chapter states
each scenario in full.

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
print(mdtable(acceptance_summary_table()))
```
Table: Comparisons and verdict by scenario

## Divergence journal

The journal lists every recorded outcome that failed acceptance, one row per outcome. Three
kinds of outcome appear: a comparison outside the criteria stated in section *Acceptance
criteria* ($r_{tol}$ = `j ACCEPT_RTOL`, $a_{tol}$ = `j ACCEPT_ATOL`), a failed test suite
run, and a required scenario that did not report. For a comparison the row carries the
computed value, the reference value, their difference and the relative error
$|x - x_{ref}| / |x_{ref}|$.

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
print(acceptance_journal_block())
```

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
# The Conclusion marks itself once its tables are rendered. A chunk that
# errored out records nothing, so a report that lost its verdict is caught by
# the required-scenario check outside the document generator. The mark is made
# before the journal is written, so that the file written here already carries
# it. `validation.jl` writes the journal again in any case.
acceptance_mark("CONCLUSION", true, "conclusion rendered")
acceptance_write_journal()
print("Full comparison log: docs/src/validation_acceptance.tsv\n\n" *
      "Divergence journal: docs/src/validation_divergences.tsv")
```

